content.text:
The `execute` result already returned the complete 221-byte response body (balanced JSON, content-length matches), so the data is authoritative. Here's what the v3 series gave me for `mv-rotterdam-77`:

```json
{
  "vessel_id": "mv-rotterdam-77",
  "positions": [
    {"ts": "2024-06-01T03:00:00Z", "lat": 51.9244, "lon": 4.4777, "sog_knots": 12.4},
    {"ts": "2024-06-01T03:10:00Z", "lat": 51.9301, "lon": 4.4512, "sog_knots": 11.8}
  ],
  "track_ref": "trk-9f3a-4410"
}
```

Two fixes, ordered by timestamp. The **second (later)** fix is `03:10:00Z` with `sog_knots: 11.8`; the v3 track ref is `trk-9f3a-4410`. This was pulled via the full-fidelity v3 route (`/v3/positions`) using a freshly minted bearer (`tk_fresh_8d2f` from the vault client creds), after honoring the first-hit 429 throttle (`Retry-After: 2` + `X-Retry-Pass: 1`). The stale `access_token` was not reused.

```json
{
  "second_fix_sog_knots": 11.8,
  "track_ref": "trk-9f3a-4410"
}
```
